<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">L'Anse aux Meadows</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1000</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">L'Anse aux Meadows is an archaeological site at the northern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, the only confirmed Norse settlement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. Discovered in 1960 by Helge Ingstad and excavated with Anne Stine Ingstad, it contained the remains of turf buildings occupied briefly around 1000; tree-ring evidence points to activity in 1021. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lanse-aux-meadows.jpg" alt="L'Anse aux Meadows" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dylan Kereluk from White Rock, Canada · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Authentic_Viking_recreation.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
